%%meta name: Investment Planning & Wealth Management System
%%meta kind: erd
%%meta version: 1.0.0
%%meta description: A wealth-management platform for an advisory firm, from the first conversation with a prospect through to the commission the firm is paid. It holds parties and the households they belong to, the advisors and teams who serve them, and the compliance file — KYC, FATCA and CRS declarations, suitability assessments, powers of attorney and signed documents — that has to be complete before any money moves. On top of that sits the planning side: goals, income, expenses, liabilities, cash flows and the scenarios run against them; a security master covering funds, equities, bonds, AIF, PMS, insurance and real estate; and the portfolios, accounts, folios, holdings and tax lots that record what a client actually owns. Recommendations are assessed for suitability and concentration, approved by someone other than their author, turned into proposals a client accepts, and executed as orders on a dealing desk. Drift against the model allocation raises a rebalance; performance is snapshotted and attributed against a benchmark; fees and commissions are reconciled against what the manufacturer paid. Every write is audited.

%% Every entity is named by exactly one category. The dashboard is built from
%% these and nothing else, so an entity left out of all of them is a table with
%% no way in.
%%category name: Party and Household; description: Legal identities, the households they belong to and the contact, nominee and mandate records attached to them; icon: Users; color: #6366f1; entities: Party, Person, Organization, Household, HouseholdMember, Client, Address, ContactPoint, Nominee, PowerOfAttorney
%%category name: Advisor and Organization; description: The firm itself — its units, advisors, teams and the households each advisor is assigned; icon: Building2; color: #0ea5e9; entities: OrganizationUnit, Advisor, AdvisorAssignment, Team, TeamMember
%%category name: CRM and Onboarding; description: Prospects, the conversations held with them, service requests raised afterwards, and the case that carries a prospect through to an active client; icon: UserPlus; color: #ec4899; entities: Prospect, Interaction, Activity, ServiceRequest, OnboardingCase
%%category name: Compliance and Identity; description: The regulatory file — KYC, FATCA and CRS declarations, suitability assessments, identity documents, signatures and the audit trail; icon: ShieldCheck; color: #f59e0b; entities: KYCRecord, KYCVerification, FATCADeclaration, CRSDeclaration, SuitabilityAssessment, IdentityDocument, ESignatureRequest, BankAccount, Document, AuditEvent, AdvancedComplianceRecord
%%category name: Financial Planning; description: The plan itself — assumptions, income, expenses, liabilities, cash flows, goals and the scenarios run against them; icon: Target; color: #14b8a6; entities: FinancialPlan, FinancialPlanAssumption, IncomeSource, Expense, Liability, CashFlow, Goal, GoalFunding, GoalProjection, Scenario, ScenarioAssumption
%%category name: Risk; description: How much risk a household says it will take, how that was assessed, and how the assessment has changed; icon: Gauge; color: #ef4444; entities: RiskAssessment, RiskProfile, RiskProfileHistory
%%category name: Security Master; description: The investable universe — instruments, their types, the houses that manage them and their prices; icon: Library; color: #8b5cf6; entities: Security, SecurityType, MutualFundScheme, AMC, ProductPrice, AssetClass, CorporateAction, Benchmark
%%category name: Accounts and Portfolio; description: What a client actually owns: accounts, folios, portfolios, holdings, lots and the valuations taken of them; icon: Wallet; color: #06b6d4; entities: InvestmentAccount, Folio, Portfolio, PortfolioAccount, Holding, HoldingLot, PortfolioValuation
%%category name: Allocation; description: The model portfolios and the per-asset-class targets they set; icon: PieChart; color: #a855f7; entities: AssetAllocationModel, AllocationTarget
%%category name: Transactions and Execution; description: Orders sent to the dealing desk, the transactions they settle into, and the standing instructions that generate them; icon: ArrowLeftRight; color: #22c55e; entities: InvestmentTransaction, Order, SIPInstruction, STPInstruction, SWPInstruction
%%category name: Recommendations and Proposals; description: What was advised, whether it was suitable, who approved it, and what the client said; icon: FileSignature; color: #3b82f6; entities: InvestmentRecommendation, RecommendationItem, SuitabilityResult, RecommendationApproval, Proposal, ClientAcceptance
%%category name: Rebalancing and Performance; description: Drift against the model, the performance measured afterwards, and the review held with the client; icon: TrendingUp; color: #10b981; entities: RebalanceRecommendation, PerformanceSnapshot, PerformanceAttribution, ClientReview
%%category name: Fees and Revenue; description: What the firm charges, what it is paid, and the reconciliation between the two; icon: Receipt; color: #eab308; entities: FeeSchedule, Commission, CommissionReconciliation, RevenueHierarchy, SubBroker
%%category name: Investment Specializations; description: Instrument-specific detail held beside the security master, and the tax consequences of disposing of it; icon: Layers; color: #64748b; entities: Equity, Bond, AIF, PMS, Insurance, RealEstate, TaxLot, CapitalGain, ExternalIntegration

